        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-10-27T18:57:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;arenson9&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"arenson9\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Nilus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nilus/48/2099_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nilus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thanks,  I looked but couldn’t find this question.  Means a flipped Dawn with several ongoing effects in play can end up playing several new villian cards in a turn and the all go off. Man that chick it tough to beat <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This is why Absolute Zero’s card (Subzero atmosphere, I think?) that causes end of turn effects to happen at the beginning of a turn can be so powerful.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>No, because in this case, the end of turn action would occur at the beginning of the turn, and then when the card is played, it’s currently the beginning of the turn, and that new card’s end of turn action will still occur at the beginning of the turn as it’s still the beginning of the turn.  Rather, Subzero Atmosphere is powerful because cards played during the play phase of the villains turn doesn’t get a chance to have its effects played as end of turn effects occur prior to the play phase.</p>",
